# Allowlist for `mypy.stubtest`, read by scripts/run-all-checks.sh and CI.
#
# The supported imports are "from host_voyager import ..." and
# "from host_voyager.oops import ...", so the stubs of those two packages describe the
# whole public API. host_voyager.oops imports the module below, which is implementation
# detail and deliberately left without a stub; stubtest reports it as "failed to find
# stubs", which this file accepts. The private _voyager module is not checked at all.
# Nothing else is accepted: a public name missing from the two stubs still fails the
# check.
host_voyager\.oops\.iss
